# TypeScript and Next.js

## Next.js
Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using APIs. This project may use conventions different from training data.

## TypeScript
Strict mode. Prefer Zod-validated JSON at project boundaries. Export types from `lib/schemas/`.

## App Router
- Server components by default; `"use client"` only when needed.
- Dynamic routes: `app/prototype/[projectSlug]/`, `app/projects/[projectSlug]/`.
- Load project data via `lib/project.ts` helpers — never inline filesystem reads in components.

## HTML and accessibility
- Semantic elements (`nav`, `main`, `section`, `table`, `button`).
- Visible focus states, keyboard-operable interactions, form labels tied to inputs.
- `aria-*` only when native semantics insufficient.
- Color contrast per WCAG AA for text and controls.

## Quality
Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run test` before requesting gate review.
